3,"LIVE - Quechua - Native Music - Quena and Quenacho - JATUM ...Kichwa language - WikipediaArchiveGrid : [Ecuador, Oriente, Lowland Quichua, 1968-1969 ...Quichua, Tena Lowland language resources | Joshua ProjectQuichua, Tena Lowland Language (QUW) – L1 & L2 Speakers ...",https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aHGMBNohRyA,"Sep 26, 2019 · Please subscribe to receive more music directly from Wuauquikuna. Visit our website wuauquikuna-official.com Wuauquikuna performs at the festivals, concerts, events and other venues throughout... Kichwa (Kichwa shimi, Runashimi, also Spanish Quichua) is a Quechuan language that includes all Quechua varieties of Ecuador and Colombia (Inga), as well as extensions into Peru. It has an estimated half million speakers. A collection of lowland Quechua music, including numerous vocals (many accompanied) and instrumental music, especially violin solos, and including many examples of music associated with ritual occasions such as death songs, chicha-drinking songs, wedding music and music from curing ceremonies. Listing of people groups speaking Quichua, Tena Lowland. Quichua, Tena Lowland dialects and alternate names. Bible and ministry resource availability. Tena Lowland Quichua is an endangered indigenous language of Ecuador. It belongs to the Quechuan language family and is part of the Quechua macrolanguage. The language is used as a first language by all adults in the ethnic community, but not all young people. It is not known to be taught in schools.","Quichua, Tena Lowland",Quechuan
